course: dictionary
lesson: 1877
title: The collarbone
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name parts of your own body, and you can find them yourself. «A cyclist could not stop in time, knocked her down, and she had a broken collarbone.» The words broken collarbone show that a bone was hurt, and the sentence says it was a bone from a fall on the road.
explain: Use the clues to find where it is. «The collarbone often breaks from a fall on the shoulder.» So the collarbone must sit near the shoulder, at the top of your body.
explain: Feel for yours. Put one finger on the top of your chest and slide it outwards towards your shoulder. The long thin bone under your skin is your collarbone. You have one on each side.
fact: Collarbone means one of two long thin bones at the front of your body, running from the top of your chest to each shoulder.
fact: Clavicle is another name for the collarbone, and you may meet it in science lessons about the skeleton.
fact: A collarbone can break in a fall onto the shoulder, and this is a common injury for children.
fact: «Most broken collarbones are treated with a sling, not a cast.»
fact: «The wishbone is two collarbones joined together.»
exercise: In «She had a broken collarbone», what was broken? | A tooth | *A bone near the shoulder | A fingernail | A toe
exercise: Where does the collarbone run? | From your knee to your ankle | From your ear to your chin | From your wrist to your elbow | *From the top of your chest to your shoulder
exercise: Which word is another name for the collarbone in science? | sling | wishbone | shoulder blade | *clavicle
test: A fall on which part of the body often breaks a collarbone? | The head | The knee | The back of the neck | *The shoulder
test: How many collarbones do you have? | *Two, one on each side | Four | Ten | One
exam: Which description fits the collarbone? | *One of two long thin bones from the top of the chest to each shoulder | A small bone in the hand | The hard shell of an egg | A soft muscle in the leg
